# THE BUNDLE IS COMMITTED, SO THE SOURCE BYTES ARE PART OF THE BUILD (2026-08-27)
#
# console/room/ is a Vite build of ui/src, committed so the gateway serves it with no Node
# at runtime, and G-ROOM-BUNDLE rebuilds ui/src and compares the emitted bytes with what is
# committed. That check is only meaningful if everyone building it starts from the same
# bytes.
#
# They did not. The exporter writes ui/src with LF; a clone on Windows checked it out as
# CRLF (`core.autocrlf=true`, and there was no .gitattributes anywhere to say otherwise).
# Multi-line template literals and JSX text keep their newlines verbatim through the
# bundler, so the two builds differed by 10 bytes and G-ROOM-BUNDLE was RED for anyone who
# cloned this repo — while passing in the tree it was built in. The toolchain was never the
# problem: vite, esbuild and the plugin all resolve to identical versions from the lock.
#
# `eol=lf` makes the checkout byte-identical on every platform, so the committed bundle is
# reproducible by whoever clones it. That is the whole point of committing it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ...except the things that must not be touched.
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.mp4  binary
*.webm binary
*.mp3  binary
*.wav  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.safetensors binary
*.gguf binary
